GAL22V10
UA6RAM01

AB1 AB2 AB3 AB4 AB5 AB6 GALSTB RCFG8 RCFG4 RCFG2 BASEA GND
RW CFGIN NC15 ACPHASE RST DB15 DB14 DB13 DB12 NC22 DRVEN VCC

; =====================================================================
; UA6 - RocHard RH800C  -  TWO-BOARD AUTOCONFIG (RAM board + HD board)
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
; Supersedes ua6_hd_b001d.  b001d presented ONLY the HD controller and
; forced UA4's base latch to (0,0,1) at reset as a static stand-in for an
; autoconfig base write that never happened: the window landed correctly
; at $200000 but the OS was never told the RAM existed.  Proven by the
; 2026-08-16 captures - one board, er_Type $D1, MEMLIST=0, identical with
; the RAM strap on and off, no second board ever enumerated.
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
; WHY THIS WORKS - the chain, from the UA4 and U14 cracks
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
; UA4 (ua4_equations.txt, i14 = /_DRVEN from this chip's pin 23):
;
;   /o23 (/_E8WIN)  = /i14 & i15 & /i20  +  /i14 & /o23
;        -> both terms need /_DRVEN LOW.  DRVEN HIGH releases /_E8WIN.
;   o16/o17/o18 (base latch -> /_CFGD15/14/13)   .oe = /i14
;        -> Hi-Z while DRVEN HIGH.  Hi-Z = transparent = CAPTURE MODE;
;           it holds whatever was on DB15/14/13 when DRVEN goes LOW.
;   /o19 (/GALCLK1, the RAM window decode) has /i14 in EVERY term
;        -> the window only decodes once DRVEN is LOW again.
;   /o21 (/_GALSTROBE) terms 3-5:  ... & i14 & /i15 & (/i9|/i10|/i11)
;        & AB16-23 = $E8
;        -> fires at $E8 ONLY while DRVEN is HIGH and a RAM size strap is
;           fitted.  That is UA4 telling us "this is a RAM-board cycle".
;
; U14 (u14_equations.txt, original, untouched):
;   /o15 (/_ROMOE2) = /i6 & /i7 & /i11 + /i8 & /o15
;                   = /_CFGADDR_MATCH & _AS & AB15=0
;   and /_CFGADDR_MATCH is U10's (74LS688) output, whose /G is /_E8WIN.
;
; So:  DRVEN HIGH -> /_E8WIN HIGH -> U10 disabled -> /_CFGADDR_MATCH HIGH
;      -> U14 releases /_ROMOE -> THE ROM STOPS DRIVING DB12-15
;      -> UA6 owns the config space and can present the RAM board.
; No original chip is modified.  Everything is done from this pin 23.
;
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
; SEQUENCE
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
;  reset            DRVEN HIGH.  ROM off, UA4 base latch in capture mode,
;                   UA4's strap-gated /_GALSTROBE armed.
;  board 1 = RAM    OS reads $E80000-$E8003E; /_GALSTROBE marks each cycle;
;                   we drive DB15-DB12 with the RAM identity.
;  base write $48   OS writes A23-A20 on D15-D12.  We drop DRVEN LOW during
;                   that cycle -> UA4's latch captures it = the RAM window.
;                   $200000 -> A23-A20 = 0010 -> latch (o16,o17,o18)=(0,0,1),
;                   which is exactly the value b001d used to force.
;  board 2 = HD     ROM is now on; the HD controller enumerates exactly as
;                   it does today (er_Type $D1, manuf 2144, product 1).
;
; RAM board identity - matches WinUAE's rochard_sub[] (memory_mid 2144,
; memory_pid 2, memory_serial 0, memory_after = false, so the RAM board is
; FIRST and fastmem_autoconfig sets chainedconfig):
;
;   er_Type   = zorroII $C0 | MEMLIST $20 | CHAINEDCONFIG $08 | size
;               2M -> $EE      4M -> $EF      8M -> $E8
;   er_Product= 2      er_Flags = 0 (WinUAE fastmem_autoconfig: flags = 0)
;   er_Manuf  = 2144 ($0860)   serial 0   InitDiagVec 0 (no diag ROM)
;
; Registers are read as two nibbles on D15-D12, at offsets R and R+2, and
; every register EXCEPT $00/$02/$40/$42 is stored one's-complemented.
; That makes almost every nibble $F, so this only has to pull bits LOW:
;
;   off  nibble  DB15 DB14 DB13 DB12   why
;   $00   E       1    1    1    0     er_Type high nibble
;   $02   E/F/8   -    -    -    -     er_Type low nibble = size:
;                                        2M $E -> 1110   (DB12 low)
;                                        4M $F -> 1111   (nothing low)
;                                        8M $8 -> 1000   (DB14/13/12 low)
;   $06   D       1    1    0    1     er_Product 2 -> $FD
;   $12   7       0    1    1    1     er_Manuf hi $08 -> $F7
;   $14   9       1    0    0    1     er_Manuf lo $60 -> $9F
;   all others $F (flags 0, serial 0, diagvec 0, reserved -> $FF)
;
; Offsets in AB6..AB1:  $00=000000  $02=000001  $06=000011
;                       $12=010001  $14=010010
;   (offset = AB6*64 + AB5*32 + AB4*16 + AB3*8 + AB2*4 + AB1*2)
;
; BOARD: game II - DIP-1 ON - DIP-2 ON - JPA1 2M, SIMM0/1 populated,
;        UA3b = ua3b_rebuild8.jed (fuse 0xC824).
; =====================================================================


; ---- /_DRVEN (pin 23) : the phase control -----------------------------
; HIGH = RAM-board phase (ROM off, UA4 latch capturing).
; LOW  = normal operation / HD-board phase (ROM on, window decoding).
;
; Term 1 - the RAM board's base write ends the RAM phase.
;   /_GALSTROBE asserted (=> $E8 cycle, DRVEN high, RAM strap fitted),
;   R/W = write, and offset $48 (base) or $4C (shut up).  $48 = AB6 & AB3,
;   $4C = AB6 & AB3 & AB2, so one term with AB2 don't-care covers both.
;   /AB1 deliberately EXCLUDES $4A - the low nibble of the base is written
;   there first, and we must stay in capture mode until $48 arrives.
;   /BASEA delays the drop until write data is valid on the bus (BASE_A is
;   _AS registered twice through U12).  ** TUNING POINT: if the captured
;   base comes out wrong, this is the timing to move. **
;
; Term 2 - self-hold, cleared only by reset.
;
; Term 3 - NO RAM CONFIGURED (all three straps high, i.e. DIP-2 off or no
;   jumper).  UA4 would then never assert /_GALSTROBE at $E8, term 1 could
;   never fire, and the HD board would never enumerate.  This drops DRVEN
;   immediately so the card behaves exactly as ua6_hd_b001d does today.
/DRVEN.T = /CFGIN & /GALSTB & /RW & AB6 & /AB5 & /AB4 & AB3 & /AB1 & /BASEA & RST
         + /CFGIN & /DRVEN & RST
         + /CFGIN & /BASEA & RST & RCFG2 & RCFG4 & RCFG8
DRVEN.E  = VCC


; ---- DB15-DB12 (pins 18-21) : the RAM board's autoconfig nibbles -------
; Enabled only during a config-space READ of the RAM board:
;   /CFGIN  - we are enabled in the autoconfig chain
;   /GALSTB - UA4 says this is an $E8 cycle with a RAM strap fitted
;   RW      - read (the OS only reads $00-$3E; writes go to $48/$4A/$4C)
;   DRVEN   - still in the RAM phase.  ESSENTIAL: after DRVEN drops,
;             /_GALSTROBE also fires for ordinary $200000 RAM accesses
;             (UA4 o21 terms 1/2/6), and without this we would drive the
;             data bus during every RAM read.
; Default is HIGH ($F); each term below pulls one bit LOW.

; DB15 low only at $12 (er_Manuf hi $F7 -> nibble 7).
/DB15.T = /AB6 & /AB5 & AB4 & /AB3 & /AB2 & AB1
DB15.E  = /CFGIN & /GALSTB & RW & DRVEN

; DB14 low at $02 when the 8M strap is fitted (nibble 8), and at $14 (9).
/DB14.T = /AB6 & /AB5 & /AB4 & /AB3 & /AB2 & AB1 & /RCFG8
        + /AB6 & /AB5 & AB4 & /AB3 & AB2 & /AB1
DB14.E  = /CFGIN & /GALSTB & RW & DRVEN

; DB13 low at $02 (8M), $06 (er_Product 2 -> $FD, nibble D) and $14 (9).
/DB13.T = /AB6 & /AB5 & /AB4 & /AB3 & /AB2 & AB1 & /RCFG8
        + /AB6 & /AB5 & /AB4 & /AB3 & AB2 & AB1
        + /AB6 & /AB5 & AB4 & /AB3 & AB2 & /AB1
DB13.E  = /CFGIN & /GALSTB & RW & DRVEN

; DB12 low at $00 (er_Type high nibble E) and at $02 for the 2M ($E) and
; 8M ($8) straps.  4M is $F, so no term - the bit stays high.
/DB12.T = /AB6 & /AB5 & /AB4 & /AB3 & /AB2 & /AB1
        + /AB6 & /AB5 & /AB4 & /AB3 & /AB2 & AB1 & /RCFG2
        + /AB6 & /AB5 & /AB4 & /AB3 & /AB2 & AB1 & /RCFG8
DB12.E  = /CFGIN & /GALSTB & RW & DRVEN


; ---- /_AC_PHASE (pin 16) : Hi-Z ---------------------------------------
; Measured inert: capture #3 (roctect_ac_ramoff2.csv.gz) shows this pin
; CONSTANT HIGH for the whole boot with 0 transitions, and its only
; destination (U11 pin 5) is not what gates the RAM path.  Left released,
; as in b001d.  Driving it LOW statically broke the HD path once already
; (ua6_hd_acp, 2026-08-05).
ACPHASE.T = VCC
ACPHASE.E = AB1 & /AB1


; ---- NC15 (pin 15), NC22 (pin 22) : unconnected pads, left Hi-Z --------
; Kept free as state nodes for a later revision if the sequence needs more
; than the single self-holding phase bit in /_DRVEN.
NC15.T = VCC
NC15.E = AB1 & /AB1
NC22.T = VCC
NC22.E = AB1 & /AB1


DESCRIPTION

UA6 two-board autoconfig: presents the RAM board first, then the HD board.

Holds /_DRVEN HIGH out of reset, which releases UA4's /_E8WIN, disables
U10, deasserts /_CFGADDR_MATCH and so makes U14 release /_ROMOE - the ROM
stops driving DB12-15 and UA6 presents a Zorro II RAM board (er_Type
$EE/$EF/$E8 for 2M/4M/8M, MEMLIST + CHAINEDCONFIG, manuf 2144, product 2).
UA4's base latch is Hi-Z throughout, so the OS's base write at offset $48
is captured directly as the RAM window position ($200000 -> (0,0,1)).
The write drops /_DRVEN, the ROM comes back on, and the HD controller
enumerates exactly as before.  No original chip is altered.

With no RAM strap fitted (DIP-2 off) /_DRVEN drops immediately and the
card behaves identically to ua6_hd_b001d.

TEST
  1. DIP-2 OFF: HD must still autoboot exactly as today.
  2. DIP-2 ON, JPA1 2M, SIMMs in bank 0: re-run the autoconfig capture
     (AUTOCONFIG_PROBE.md).  Expect TWO boards - first er_Type $EE with
     MEMLIST set, manuf 2144 product 2, then er_Type $D1 as today.
  3. Check the base write at $48 reads nibble 2 (A23-A20 = 0010) and that
     UA4's latch (CFGD15/14/13) ends up (0,0,1).
  4. ATK / Workbench: 2 MB Fast should now appear in the Kickstart memory
     scan and in "avail".
